<title>BELGIUM: Alardo charge knocks Spadel in the red.</title>
<headline>Alardo charge knocks Spadel in the red.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(in million Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net (ex. minorities)   loss  65    vs   128 profit</p>
<p>    Exceptional costs		     169    vs   nil</p>
<p>Note - Belgian beverage firm Spadel said the exceptional loss was related to the temporary halt of the activities of its Portuguese mineral water bottling unit Alardo. Spadel warned about the 169 million charge on March 28.  </p>
<p>    Cons turnover			 8,345    vs 8,920</p>
<p>    Pretax cashflow		     1,142    vs 1,246</p>
<p>    Pretax operating profit	     255    vs   255</p>
<p>    Taxes				     150    vs   126</p>
<p>    Net dividend (in francs)	    366    vs   366</p>
<p>NOTE - Spadel said the number of litres sold fell by 7.6 percent, mainly due to the fact that the hot summer of 1995 was not repeated in 1996. However, it benefited from the price fall of PET plastics.</p>
<p>In March Portuguese authorities ordered production and sale of Alardo water be halted after it was found to contain plankton. Alardo water was withdrawn from retailers' shelves. Production was halted for a total 10 days.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
